nia. After setting aside Hungary (22-0) and the United States (29-1), Germany encountered somewhat more resistance in the final pool. The last match. against Austria, played in a packed Olympic Stadium, was relatively closely contested, but the Germans still emerged victorious, 10-6."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In 1938, Germany and Austria also finished 1-2 at the inaugural World championships (indoor handball). Later that year, the first outdoor handball world championship was also won by the Germans. Austria was absent, as it had been annexed by Germany earlier in the year. Apart from eight German Olympic champions, the World champion team also featured Austrian " [:a {:href "/athletes/31848"} "Poldl Wohlrab"] ", who had won a silver medal in Berlin."] "\n"] [:button {:id "button236721", :class "btn btn-default"} "Details"] [:script {} "$('#button236721').click(splits)"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Games"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Goals / Saves"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Wins"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Draws"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Losses"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Points"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Goals"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "Germany"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "5"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "96"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "–"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "–"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "–"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "–"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display